) 5. c3
{ [%eval 0.02] Supports d4 and also stops ...Nb4, which would hit the bishop. The queen gets c2, and the knight on b1 will go to d2. This is the full Colle setup. }
( 5. b3
{ [%eval 0.16] The Colle-Zukertort. The bishop goes to b2 and the c-pawn stays at home, so White does not need c3. The long diagonal is open, and White can follow with Ne5 and an attack on the kingside. Keep the Greek gift Bxh7+ in mind, but check it concretely, because it often fails. }
