{ [%eval 0.08] The knight comes to d2 and e4 is ready. } ) 5... Nc6
{ [%eval 0.22] Black develops. } 6. Nbd2
{ [%eval 0.08] The knight comes to d2 so that the bishop and the knights all support e4. Note that it blocks the queen's defence of the bishop on d3, so be careful about tricks against that bishop before you castle. }
6... Bd6 { [%eval 0.26] Black develops and aims at h2. } 7. O-O
{ [%eval 0.15] White castles. } 7... O-O { [%eval 0.12] Black castles. } 8.
dxc5 { [%eval 0.13] White takes and opens the d-file for the break to come. }
8... Bxc5 { [%eval 0.12] Black recaptures. } 9. e4
{ [%eval 0.00] [%cal Ge3e4] The point of the whole system. White castles first, takes on c5 to deflect Black's bishop, and then pushes e4 with the pieces all supporting it. If White never gets e4 in, Black's ...e5 equalises and the game goes dead, which is the main reason the Colle fails. }
9... dxe4 { [%eval 0.51] Black takes. } 10. Nxe4
{ [%eval 0.53] White recaptures with the knight and has a lead in activity. }
10... Be7 $14
{ [%eval 0.53] Black retreats the bishop and keeps the position solid. } *
